- Findings may not generalize beyond the studied sites, period, technology, or workload range.
- Faster completion may reflect deferral, premature closure, lower quality, or costs shifted downstream; guardrail outcomes are therefore essential.
- Correlated operational changes may leave several explanations observationally indistinguishable. Such cases should be reported as unresolved and used to motivate a future randomized or phased intervention.
